## Update: extensions/zip-code-widget/shopify.extension.toml

Read the current toml file. It likely registers one block. Add a second block registration for the cart validator.

The format should follow the existing block registration. For Shopify Theme App Extensions, multiple blocks are registered like:

```toml
[[blocks]]
  type = "local/cart-validator"
  name = "Zip Code Checker — Cart Validator"
  limit = 1
```

Or it may use a different format. Read the actual file and match the existing format exactly.

If the current format uses a single `[blocks]` section (not `[[blocks]]`), check the Shopify TAE toml format. The new block must be registered so Shopify recognizes it.

---

## Update: extensions/zip-code-widget/locales/en.default.json

Read the current file and add any needed localization keys for the cart validator, following the existing pattern. If the file is minimal, just add:
```json
"cart_validator": {
  "title": "Zip Code Checker — Cart Validator",
  "warning_title": "Delivery Not Available",
  "dismiss": "Dismiss"
}
```

---

## NO TypeScript check needed (liquid/toml files, not TypeScript)

